{"id":"a52d75a807d5cff8","group":"93","path":"93/93-thm-completeness-propositional.md","title":"Godel Completeness Theorem","display":"Godel Completeness Theorem","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Algebraizable Logics","book_abbrev":"93","label":"93-thm-completeness-propositional","aliases":["93-thm-completeness-propositional"],"display":"Godel Completeness Theorem","depends_on":["[[93-df-classical-propositional-calculus]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Algebraizable Logics"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"93"},{"key":"label","html":"93-thm-completeness-propositional"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>93-thm-completeness-propositional</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"Godel Completeness Theorem"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"e3c8f5c9e577b791\" href=\"?note=e3c8f5c9e577b791\" title=\"93-df-classical-propositional-calculus\">93-df-classical-propositional-calculus</a></span></div>"}],"html":"<h1 id=\"thm-completeness-propositional-—-Gödel-Completeness-Theorem\">thm-completeness-propositional — Gödel Completeness Theorem</h1>\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{CPLPres}_{93}(\\mathcal P,\\mathsf L,\\mathcal L)\">\\(\\mathrm{CPLPres}_{93}(\\mathcal P,\\mathsf L,\\mathcal L)\\)</span> is the concrete three-scheme Hilbert calculus of <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"e3c8f5c9e577b791\" href=\"?note=e3c8f5c9e577b791\" title=\"93-df-classical-propositional-calculus\">93-df-classical-propositional-calculus</a>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"F^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93}\">\\(F^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\vdash^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93}\">\\(\\vdash^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93}\\)</span> are its formula set and proof-induced relation; <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\models^{\\mathbf2,\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93}\">\\(\\models^{\\mathbf2,\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93}\\)</span> is its independently defined two-valued semantic consequence relation.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}completeness\\text{-}propositional}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{CPLPres}_{93}(\\mathcal P,\\mathsf L,\\mathcal L)\\to\n\\forall\\Gamma\\subseteq F^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93}\\;\n\\forall\\varphi\\in F^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93}\\;\n\\bigl(\\Gamma\\vdash^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93}\\varphi\n\\leftrightarrow\\Gamma\\models^{\\mathbf2,\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93}\\varphi\\bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}completeness\\text{-}propositional}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{CPLPres}_{93}(\\mathcal P,\\mathsf L,\\mathcal L)\\to\n\\forall\\Gamma\\subseteq F^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93}\\;\n\\forall\\varphi\\in F^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93}\\;\n\\bigl(\\Gamma\\vdash^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93}\\varphi\n\\leftrightarrow\\Gamma\\models^{\\mathbf2,\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93}\\varphi\\bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>The theorem now compares a separately defined proof calculus with two-valued semantics; soundness and completeness are the conclusion, not part of a prose description of the calculus. The presentation predicate ties the proof-theoretic and language objects to the same Boolean formula carrier.</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"thm-completeness-propositional-—-Gödel-Completeness-Theorem","text":"thm-completeness-propositional — Gödel Completeness Theorem","level":1},{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"93-df-classical-propositional-calculus","status":"resolved","id":"e3c8f5c9e577b791","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[93-df-classical-propositional-calculus]]","embed":false},{"target":"93-df-classical-propositional-calculus","status":"resolved","id":"e3c8f5c9e577b791","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{CPLPres}_{93}(\\mathcal P,\\mathsf L,\\mathcal L)$ is the concrete three-scheme Hilbert calculus of [[93-df-classical-propositional-calculus]].","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\mathrm{CPLPres}_{93}(\\mathcal P,\\mathsf L,\\mathcal L)","display":false},{"tex":"F^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93}","display":false},{"tex":"\\vdash^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93}","display":false},{"tex":"\\models^{\\mathbf2,\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}completeness\\text{-}propositional}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{CPLPres}_{93}(\\mathcal P,\\mathsf L,\\mathcal L)\\to\n\\forall\\Gamma\\subseteq F^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93}\\;\n\\forall\\varphi\\in F^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93}\\;\n\\bigl(\\Gamma\\vdash^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93}\\varphi\n\\leftrightarrow\\Gamma\\models^{\\mathbf2,\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93}\\varphi\\bigr)","display":true}],"bytes":1363,"backlinks":[],"outgoing":["e3c8f5c9e577b791"]}